Appendix H: Feasibility Checks and Power

H.1 Feasibility of the detection curve. Ninety-eight EvoClaw milestones may generate too few regression instances to estimate a heavy tail. Phase A must report the number of regressions with observed kill outcomes at several test budgets. If that number is too small, the direct q(n) curve is deferred to the Phase 2 expansion. The hypothesis is labeled a conjecture, not a conclusion.

H.2 Power. At 98 milestones the standard errors are too large to resolve the susceptibility peak (C.3) or the interaction coefficients in \hat R_t with narrow intervals. Phase A must expand to tens of repositories before the Phase 2 falsification tests can discriminate between percolation and its nulls. The expansion is a precondition, not a refinement.

H.3 Depth. The effective depth L_t is the operative quantity in Proposition A.1. Phase A must report L_t for every repository, because finite depth bounds the saturation level even when R^{w}_{\mathrm{DP}}>1. Repositories with large L_t are the most discriminating for the peak prediction.

